method.description:
Converts [param data] to YAML text, and saves it to a file at [param path]. Returns a [YAMLResult] containing the generated YAML string or error information.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var save_data = {
    "player": {
        "name": "Hero",
        "level": 10,
        "position": [25, 48]
    },
    "quests_completed": ["Rats in the Cellar", "Lost Artifact"]
}

var result = YAML.save_file(save_data, "user://save_game.yaml")
if result.has_error():
    return push_error("Save failed: " + result.get_error())

print("Game saved successfully!")
[/codeblock]

Simplified version of [method load_file] that returns the parsed data directly, or [code]null[/code] on error.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var settings = YAML.try_load_file("user://settings.yaml")
if settings:
    apply_settings(settings)
else:
    create_default_settings()
[/codeblock]

Simplified version of [method save_file] that returns [code]true[/code] on success, [code]false[/code] on error.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var player_progress = {
    "level_completed": 5,
    "collectibles": 28,
    "unlocked_abilities": ["double_jump", "dash"]
}

if YAML.try_save_file(player_progress, "user://progress.yaml"):
    print("Progress saved!")
else:
    print("Failed to save progress")
[/codeblock]

Simplified version of [method stringify] that returns the YAML string directly, or an empty string on error.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var npc = {
    "name": "Merchant",
    "dialog": "Welcome to my shop!",
    "shop_items": ["Potion", "Map", "Torch"]
}

var yaml_text = YAML.try_stringify(npc)
if !yaml_text.is_empty():
    print("YAML text:\n", yaml_text)
[/codeblock]

Validates YAML syntax without performing a full parse. Returns a [YAMLResult] containing error information.
Faster than [method parse] when you only need to check validity.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var user_input = get_text_from_user()

var result = YAML.validate(user_input)
if result.has_error():
    return push_error(result.get_error())

# YAML has valid syntax, proceed with parsing
[/codeblock]

Validates YAML syntax in a file without performing a full parse. Returns a [YAMLResult] containing error information.
Useful for quickly checking file format validity.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var result = YAML.validate_file("user://mod_config.yaml")
if result.has_error():
    print("Mod configuration has syntax errors: " + result.get_error())
    print("Please fix your mod configuration file.")
else:
    print("Mod configuration syntax is valid.")
[/codeblock]
